            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this recipe as an appetizer. I poured it over cream cheese and served ot with wheat crackers. It was a big hit, and the flavor got better with age."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tfnoles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Didn't use the orange peel. Used the zest and some orange juice. We enjoyed it.",
            "datePublished": "2019-11-29T03:24:23.050Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TBIRDTECH"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been used this very same recipe for years... The only recent change I've made is using granulated Stevia (cup for cup) instead of white sugar. Still just as amazing &amp; no one misses the insulin spikes or any of those bad carbs. Actually no one has noticed a difference in taste",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-14T19:34:59.293Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "suthernfancy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy to make. Very tasty not too sweet. I did not add any orange peel or zest. I used 2/3 cup orange juice and 2/3 cup water for water and orange liqueur. Recipe makes 2 pints. I hope you don't mind I added my photos when cooking your recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-08T11:01:56.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stacey Baldridge"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made some of this chutney III and put it in little mason jars to give out as gifts...I got 6.5 jars (half pint). I just tested it out, and it tastes great! Of course, cranberries are a little tart/bitter, but if it had been on turkey instead of my fork, and hot, it would be great!! I'm excited to try it. 2 tips: Grate the orange peel...I did about 1tbsp, and that's really all I thought it needed. 2. For the orange liquer, I used half of the orange I grated, and a drop of vodka. Great recipe, super easy to make. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-03T15:14:23.123Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LorieD"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very nice recipe. I skipped the alcohol, and substituted 1 cup fresh squeezed oj for the water. Not too sweet, slightly tart.",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-02T12:02:48.503Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tanya Rosario"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a nice alternative to the normal cranberry sauce. Even my mother enjoyed it and she is not a fan of cranberry sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2009-12-22T11:56:53.637Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mommys3"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipie is fabulous. My kids loved it!!! I used less sugar about 1 1/2 cups I could not believe how good it is I used pineapple rum instead of orange liqueour. Soooo good! this is the perfect recipe to begin. It is something that I can easily add to or change as needed. Thanks.",
            "datePublished": "2008-11-30T10:55:17.550Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "gemgirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Shouldn't it be orange zest instead of orange peel? Especially with navel oranges, since they have really thick peels. I can't even imagine how awful an entire orange peel could make ANY recipe. \nI will try this; it sounds good.",
            "datePublished": "2008-01-29T09:50:41.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "1"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used the peel of one whole orange chopped, I used a navel orange, and it was so bitter the sauce wasn't even edible. Then I made a second batch without the orange and combined it and it was still horrible, I think a much smaller portion of perhaps just a tablespoon or 2 of fresh grated orange peel would have been better. I ended up serving it at my family Thanksgiving dinner with 16 people, total flop, no one liked it.",
            "datePublished": "2004-11-26T11:21:07.437Z"
          }
